 ## Overview
-Six packages in one repo. `qdata` is the Python data library. It downloads Sharadar prices, corporate actions, tickers and S&P 500 membership into an append-only local store where every record carries its first-known date, and each completed run commits a read-only data version. It also runs the validation checks and the Yahoo cross-check, and gives research code a point-in-time reader. `qrisk` is the S2 variance study. It reads windows from `qdata`'s point-in-time reader, builds covariance estimates and long-only portfolios, scores them out of sample, and writes each study run to its own folder. `qfeat` is the S3 feature study. It reuses `qrisk`'s windows and factor counts to build next-month residual targets, computes price and volume features, trains a walk-forward model, tests every feature claim against chance, and allows one holdout run per registered feature list. `qfcst` is the S4 forecasting stage. It trains a compact neural forecaster locally on `qfeat`'s panel and S3's surviving features, builds forecast portfolios beside `qrisk`'s classical ones, and keeps a simulated paper book that every refresh marks. `qserver` is the local backend: it runs `qdata`'s downloads and checks as worker processes, reads study results through `qrisk`, and serves an HTTP + Server-Sent Events API bound to localhost. `explorer` (TypeScript + React) is the browser app. It talks to `qserver` only through that API, with types generated from `qserver`'s OpenAPI schema.
